  "body": "Hi,\r\n\r\nI've installed synapse on Debian Stable (Jessie) from the matrix repository.\r\nI've configured `homeserver.yaml` to use my ldap server.\r\n\r\nThe first time I launched it, it said that ldap3 was not found. I didn't find any documentation on how to install synapse, but I understood that I had to install `ldap3` package with `python-pip`.\r\n\r\nWhen I launched it, I had the following error : \r\n`AttributeError: 'module' object has no attribute 'AUTH_SIMPLE'`\r\n\r\nIt appears that python can't find `AUTH_SIMPLE` from `ldap3`. Indeed, when we read the [ldap3 changelog](https://ldap3.readthedocs.io/changelog.html), we see that : \r\n\r\n> 2.0.7 2016.10.27\r\n>  * FIRST RELEASE OF LDAP3 V2\r\n>  * ...\r\n>  * The following older constants in ldap3 have been removed, please use the suggested ones:\r\n>     * AUTH_ANONYMOUS = ANONYMOUS\r\n>     * AUTH_SIMPLE = SIMPLE\r\n>     * AUTH_SASL = SASL \r\n\r\nI've found a workaround by running `pip install ldap3==1.4.7` which is the latest version of ldap3 before the v2.\r\n\r\nI don't know what you want to do (update `ldap_auth_provider.py` or keep the old version of ldap3) or even if I missed something (an instruction in the documentation, a `requirement.txt` file) and so this issue should be useless.\r\n\r\nI can't start working on a patch (if you want to upgrade to ldap3 v2) before 2 weeks and I'm not sure that this hypothetical fix will work, so everyone wanting to fix this issue is welcome :)",
